---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro'
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro'
import editorImage from '../../assets/kieli-editor.webp'
import { pageContentTransition, viewTransitionNameFromPath } from '../../utils/viewTransitionName'

const pageTitle = 'Kieli'
const pageDescription = 'An open-source, self-hosted workspace for product copy and translations.'
const titleTransitionName = viewTransitionNameFromPath(Astro.url.pathname)
const repositoryUrl = 'https://github.com/brnrd/Kieli'
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main
			id="main-content"
			tabindex="-1"
			class="content stack kieli-page"
			transition:name="page-content"
			transition:animate={pageContentTransition}
		>
			<article class="stack">
				<header class="stack">
					<p class="meta">Build</p>
					<h1
						class="transition-title"
						style={`--view-transition-name: ${titleTransitionName};`}
						transition:name={titleTransitionName}
					>
						{pageTitle}
					</h1>
					<p>{pageDescription}</p>
					<nav class="project-links" aria-label="Kieli links">
						<a href={repositoryUrl}>View on GitHub</a>
						<a href={`${repositoryUrl}#get-started`}>Get started</a>
					</nav>
				</header>

				<p>
					The words in an app need somewhere to live. Kieli brings source copy, translation keys and
					every language into one shared workspace, so product teams and developers can keep them
					organised and ship them through their existing build pipeline.
				</p>

				<figure class="stack editor-preview">
					<a href={editorImage.src} aria-label="View the full-size Kieli editor screenshot">
						<Image
							src={editorImage}
							alt="Kieli’s translation editor with English source copy, French and Dutch translations, missing translations, and freshness indicators."
							widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
							sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px"
						/>
					</a>
					<figcaption>
						Source copy and translations together in the editor. Sample project from the{' '}
						<a href={`${repositoryUrl}#a-focused-home-for-your-copy`}>Kieli repository</a>.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<section class="stack" aria-labelledby="copy">
					<h2 id="copy">Keep every language in view</h2>
					<p>
						Projects, namespaces and tags give copy some structure. The editor keeps language values
						together and flags missing or outdated translations when the source changes. A shared
						glossary and previous wording help keep terminology consistent, while placeholder checks
						and translation history make changes easier to catch and recover.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="stack" aria-labelledby="workflow">
					<h2 id="workflow">Work with your app</h2>
					<p>
						Import existing localisation files or Lokalise exports, then use the CLI to push source
						strings and pull translations into your codebase. JSON, YAML, gettext, Apple and Android
						formats are among the{' '}
						<a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/file-formats.md`}>supported formats</a>. CI
						can require current, valid translations before a build goes through.
					</p>
					<p>
						An optional <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/mcp.md`}>MCP connection</a>{' '}
						lets Claude Code work with project context and selected target languages. Editing and publication
						stay explicit; Kieli has no built-in automatic translation service.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="stack" aria-labelledby="hosting">
					<h2 id="hosting">Your copy, your infrastructure</h2>
					<p>
						Kieli is MIT licensed and designed for self-hosting. Try it locally with Node.js and
						SQLite, or run it for a team using the included Docker image or AWS templates. Built-in
						accounts and SSO are available, with project roles and separate credentials for
						integrations.
					</p>
					<p>
						The <a href={`${repositoryUrl}#get-started`}>setup guide</a> covers the local demo and team
						deployment. Explore the{' '}
						<a href={`${repositoryUrl}#documentation`}>documentation</a> for imports, source sync, access
						control and recovery.
					</p>
				</section>

				<p><a href="/">Back to home</a></p>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.kieli-page h1 {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.project-links {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		font-family: var(--font-label);
		font-size: 0.76rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.editor-preview img {
		inline-size: 100%;
		border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
	}

	.editor-preview figcaption {
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--color-ink-muted);
	}
</style>
